title: ml-meta-perf
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mário
    family-names: Antunes
    email: mario.antunes@av.it.pt
    affiliation: Instituto de Telecomunicações, University of Aveiro
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6504-9441'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/mariolpantunes/ml-meta-perf'
abstract: >-
  Interpretable linear meta-models that predict the Matthews Correlation
  Coefficient of a classifier from dataset and model meta-features. Equations
  take the form MCC = w1*t1 + w2*t2 + ..., where each term is a simple
  expression over one to three raw features and each weight is stated in the
  features' own units. Terms are drawn from a filtered candidate library,
  screened by paired Pearson and Spearman correlation, and selected by beam
  search with ridge refitting. Four equations are reported across three
  descriptor scopes: E1 uses dataset descriptors alone; E2 uses model
  descriptors alone; and E3-Valid and E3-MAX use both. E3-Valid selects a
  compact equation before the first sustained plateau in validation performance,
  whereas E3-MAX maximises the minimum R² over the four evaluated protocols.
  Validation includes
  leave-one-dataset-out, leave-one-model-out, and the stricter protocol that
  removes every row sharing the held-out pair's dataset or model. The leakage
  induced by random k-fold splitting on grouped meta-data is quantified rather
  than assumed away.
keywords:
  - meta-learning
  - algorithm-selection
  - symbolic-regression
  - sparse-regression
  - interpretability
  - matthews-correlation-coefficient
  - model-selection
